                        ],
                        "form": "земляке́"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "4ef2c2bb-7084-438e-a8dc-ceaf0415a6af",
                        "entry_id": "0895631a-a743-3c43-8c3a-db348d1cef31",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "prepositional"
                        ],
                        "form": "земляка́х"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7e39408b-dfe6-34dc-b960-653ba13cc2d7",
                        "entry_id": "0895631a-a743-3c43-8c3a-db348d1cef31",
                        "glosses": [
                            "человек, рождённый с кем-нибудь в одной местности, области, государстве"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "46d85e4b-bfad-4ab0-9478-c4466d2b68cb",
                                "sense_id": "7e39408b-dfe6-34dc-b960-653ba13cc2d7",
                                "text": "Так донской казак Александр Ефимов, земляк великого Шолохова, повоевал в небе надёжной ильюшинской шашкой — штурмовиком Ил-2."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b6da8501-5130-380e-aed3-6d3558c1e990",
                        "entry_id": "0895631a-a743-3c43-8c3a-db348d1cef31",
                        "glosses": [
                            "фамильярное обращение к соотечественникам своего социального круга"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed5375ea-0c7a-47cc-aed4-dd67e17a2a99",
                                "sense_id": "b6da8501-5130-380e-aed3-6d3558c1e990",
                                "text": "Слышь, земляк, ― обратился он ко мне, ― полезем мы с тобой первыми…"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "44d371bd-5488-4586-ade1-ff69566a045c",
                        "source_entry_id": "0895631a-a743-3c43-8c3a-db348d1cef31",
                        "target_lang_word": "compatriot",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "compatriot",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f06d0701-6d1d-34ee-8c21-d2e2aa1f6b47",
                                        "entry_id": "6efc10eb-d2b9-31bb-abab-9d283acd15a8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Somebody from one's own country."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "293a2d9b-f24e-4052-9c49-5a9a79cc4cc0",
                                                "sense_id": "f06d0701-6d1d-34ee-8c21-d2e2aa1f6b47",
                                                "text": "And this, perhaps, might have been anticipated; for, as varieties, in order to become in any degree permanent, necessarily have to struggle with the other inhabitants of the country, the species which are already dominant will be the most likely to yield offspring which, though in some slight degree modified, will still inherit those advantages that enabled their parents to become dominant over their compatriots."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a682905a-a087-4285-8da4-12a2a7e7e274",
                                                "sense_id": "f06d0701-6d1d-34ee-8c21-d2e2aa1f6b47",
                                                "text": "the distrust with which they felt themselves to be regarded by their compatriots in America"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3cd9554-89df-4d2d-82d0-7d3807d761b9",
                                                "sense_id": "f06d0701-6d1d-34ee-8c21-d2e2aa1f6b47",
                                                "text": "However Russian Pavlyuchenko stunned his compatriots with an unstoppable 25-yard drive into the top corner."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "compatriot",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61d634e6-f315-3325-94e6-39200bbea382",
                                        "entry_id": "644f680a-d501-3ba5-916e-88686b560d9b",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of the same country; especially, being countrymen and having a common sentiment of patriotism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "37e2ebb9-e921-47a7-a024-f09b448aa09c",
                                                "sense_id": "61d634e6-f315-3325-94e6-39200bbea382",
                                                "text": "She [Britain] rears to Freedom an undaunted Race: / Compatriot zealous, hoſpitable, kind, […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "70f79d9c-4699-4ef7-a953-df386d9a1973",
                        "source_entry_id": "0895631a-a743-3c43-8c3a-db348d1cef31",
                        "target_lang_word": "countryman",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "countryman",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6f3e152a-24cc-3e1c-8d04-bce434bd79fb",
                                        "entry_id": "8c6179b2-d27c-3ed9-9193-afc53b037262",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Somebody from a certain country."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3dd11f9c-77a1-37ac-8edf-601a6af8a68e",
                                        "entry_id": "8c6179b2-d27c-3ed9-9193-afc53b037262",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Somebody from one's own country; a fellow countryman."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2f9fa33-e08f-4240-8cc7-9a4b34eea867",
                                                "sense_id": "3dd11f9c-77a1-37ac-8edf-601a6af8a68e",
                                                "text": "Friends, Romans, Countrymen, lend me your ears: / I come to bury Cæſar, not to praiſe him:"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12e3aa06-1c00-48f2-a63a-3e2082533b5d",
                                                "sense_id": "3dd11f9c-77a1-37ac-8edf-601a6af8a68e",
                                                "text": "You don’t need to wait. Here, there she is. There, there she is right now, embodying the harsh irony that is her existence, because at that moment next week, she will be a queen with fake power visiting a fake kingdom which arguably has more impact on the lives of her countrymen than she does."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d8cba247-60fe-3c05-a8c2-d7772af746b9",
                                        "entry_id": "8c6179b2-d27c-3ed9-9193-afc53b037262",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A man who is a country dweller, especially a follower of country pursuits."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c333d3e7-f4d2-37a8-a651-4382bcd58c09",
                                        "entry_id": "8c6179b2-d27c-3ed9-9193-afc53b037262",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A settled person, as opposed to a traveller."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Ireland"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2af6d5c0-1c78-4c2d-ab8e-0023d16a6f1c",
                        "source_entry_id": "0895631a-a743-3c43-8c3a-db348d1cef31",
                        "target_lang_word": "Landsmann",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Landsmann",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3efc9757-d838-3af3-81f2-79b2e091e8db",
                                        "entry_id": "a47f530e-57eb-3874-b132-3ddbdad4b2dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Einwohner eines Landes"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "683e2e71-a99e-4ae0-a9e4-cbb52ff18053",
                                                "sense_id": "3efc9757-d838-3af3-81f2-79b2e091e8db",
                                                "text": "Er war französischer Landsmann."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9518cce-834e-4cf4-ad71-639f7e1e5369",
                                                "sense_id": "3efc9757-d838-3af3-81f2-79b2e091e8db",
                                                "text": "Und was sind Sie für ein Landsmann? — Ich bin Schwabe!"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "585d58ea-022d-3bae-a18f-80fcd27a87a7",
                                        "entry_id": "a47f530e-57eb-3874-b132-3ddbdad4b2dd",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Person, die aus dem gleichen Land wie der Sprechende bzw. aus einem genannten Land kommt"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f1be0fbe-084d-4e99-a127-c36a55cab044",
                                                "sense_id": "585d58ea-022d-3bae-a18f-80fcd27a87a7",
                                                "text": "Es stellte sich bald heraus, dass mein Gesprächspartner ein Landsmann war und wir auch deutsch miteinander sprechen konnten."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0a8778c9-3089-49db-8860-10b6af02ff20",
                                                "sense_id": "585d58ea-022d-3bae-a18f-80fcd27a87a7",
                                                "text": "„Wir wurden zwar Deutschländer genannt, aber die Türken sahen uns als Landsleute, die jederzeit zurückkonnten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bd26a688-3368-4b39-8a14-c348271e9036",
                                                "sense_id": "585d58ea-022d-3bae-a18f-80fcd27a87a7",
                                                "text": "„Doch der erfahrene Reisende versteht seine Landsleute nur zu gut.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74b80e78-7314-4345-b1c1-ee5185a5a6ca",
                                                "sense_id": "585d58ea-022d-3bae-a18f-80fcd27a87a7",
                                                "text": "„Bald musste ich feststellen, dass viele Landsleute dieses Mannes dessen Gesinnung teilten.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3f6c4f82-a121-4f7d-9822-a25b61bdfb4f",
                                                "sense_id": "585d58ea-022d-3bae-a18f-80fcd27a87a7",
                                                "text": "„Der Gouverneur hatte mit seinen Begründungen nicht unrecht gehabt, die Mitmenschlichkeit verlangte, mich meines Landsmanns anzunehmen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25ebbf37-0a96-4f49-9e96-74e1e3324dcd",
                                                "sense_id": "585d58ea-022d-3bae-a18f-80fcd27a87a7",
                                                "text": "„In diesem Zusammenhang fiel Claire auf, daß Hector Burch und John D. John junior ihre einzigen echten Landsleute in diesem Kreis waren, nämlich geborene Amerikaner.“."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b667a8d4-ef70-4c91-b217-ca644238763e",
                                                "sense_id": "585d58ea-022d-3bae-a18f-80fcd27a87a7",
                                                "text": "„Dies entpuppte sich aber als schwerer als erwartet, nicht nur aufgrund meiner linguistischen Untauglichkeit, sondern weil ich ständig auf meine Landsmänner traf.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
